Article 23

(1) In addition to general investigating officials, investigation of criminal acts of violence against women and children in this Regional Regulation may also be conducted by Civil Servant Investigators whose appointment is in accordance with laws and regulations.

(2) Civil Servant Investigators as referred to in paragraph (1), are authorized to:

a. receive reports or complaints from a person regarding the existence of criminal acts of violence against women and children;

b. take first action at that time at the scene and conduct examination;

c. interrogate a suspect and examine the suspect's identity;

d. seize objects and/or documents;

e. take fingerprints and photograph a person;

f. summon persons to be heard and examined as suspects or witnesses;

g. bring in experts required in connection with the examination of the case;

h. cease investigation after receiving instructions from the General Investigator that there is insufficient evidence, or the incident does not constitute a criminal act and subsequently through the General Investigator notify such matter to the public prosecutor, the suspect or their family; and/or

i. take other actions necessary for the smooth investigation of criminal acts of violence against women and children, which according to law can be accounted for.

(3) Investigators as referred to in paragraph (2), shall notify the commencement of investigation and submit the results of their investigation to the public prosecutor through the Investigating Official of the Indonesian National Police, in accordance with the provisions stipulated in the Criminal Procedure Code.

